1
00:00:00,245 --> 00:00:03,145
AI assistants have started shopping for people.

2
00:00:03,145 --> 00:00:05,220
But PayPal's agent checkout is built

3
00:00:05,220 --> 00:00:07,370
for merchants with a website store.

4
00:00:07,370 --> 00:00:09,207
Rosa bakes from her kitchen.

5
00:00:09,207 --> 00:00:10,608
She has no website.

6
00:00:10,608 --> 00:00:12,482
She has this sheet of paper.

7
00:00:12,482 --> 00:00:15,807
In a US Census survey, 47 percent of food

8
00:00:15,807 --> 00:00:18,232
and lodging businesses had no website.

9
00:00:18,232 --> 00:00:21,750
An assistant can't order from a sheet of paper.

10
00:00:22,678 --> 00:00:24,715
Shelfie starts with one photo.

11
00:00:24,715 --> 00:00:28,133
Rosa snaps her price list, and Claude reads it.

12
00:00:29,945 --> 00:00:32,470
Shelfie only asks about what it isn't sure of,

13
00:00:32,470 --> 00:00:35,520
like a price written as two for seven dollars.

14
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:37,520
Rosa adds her PayPal email,

15
00:00:37,520 --> 00:00:39,632
so buyers pay her directly.

16
00:00:39,632 --> 00:00:42,958
Every item becomes a product in PayPal's catalog.

17
00:00:42,958 --> 00:00:45,333
In our tests, photo to live shop took

18
00:00:45,333 --> 00:00:48,300
8 to 14 seconds of machine time.

19
00:00:49,562 --> 00:00:52,075
One more photo, of her display case.

20
00:00:52,075 --> 00:00:55,617
Claude finds each item in it, and crops its photo.

21
00:00:56,870 --> 00:00:58,595
The shop gets an agent door,

22
00:00:58,595 --> 00:01:00,395
and a card for the counter.

23
00:01:00,395 --> 00:01:01,720
Regulars scan it,

24
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:04,850
or give the shop's link to their own assistant.

25
00:01:05,128 --> 00:01:06,528
This is Claude Code,

26
00:01:06,528 --> 00:01:09,103
given nothing but the shop's web address.

27
00:01:09,103 --> 00:01:11,528
The page tells it where the agent door is.

28
00:01:11,528 --> 00:01:13,853
It reads the menu, places the order,

29
00:01:13,853 --> 00:01:16,958
and hands back a PayPal approval link.

30
00:01:21,287 --> 00:01:22,912
Buyers without an assistant get

31
00:01:22,912 --> 00:01:24,775
one right on the shop page.

32
00:01:24,775 --> 00:01:26,962
This buyer wants almond croissants,

33
00:01:26,962 --> 00:01:29,024
and mentions a nut allergy.

34
00:01:29,024 --> 00:01:31,812
The assistant warns that they contain nuts.

35
00:01:31,812 --> 00:01:35,342
The buyer confirms, and it places the order.

36
00:01:38,128 --> 00:01:40,978
The buyer logs in to PayPal and approves.

37
00:01:40,978 --> 00:01:43,291
Shelfie captures the payment, and the money

38
00:01:43,291 --> 00:01:47,383
lands in Rosa's own PayPal account, not ours.

39
00:01:49,662 --> 00:01:51,712
And agents can't set prices.

40
00:01:51,712 --> 00:01:54,492
The server checks that, not the model.

41
00:01:55,845 --> 00:01:58,908
Rosa's dashboard shows the order as paid.

42
00:01:58,908 --> 00:02:01,332
A Claude agent reads PayPal's record

43
00:02:01,332 --> 00:02:03,895
of the order through the PayPal Agent Toolkit,

44
00:02:03,895 --> 00:02:05,420
and writes her a brief.

45
00:02:05,420 --> 00:02:07,220
It catches the nut allergy,

46
00:02:07,220 --> 00:02:10,325
so she can check with the buyer before shipping.

47
00:02:11,653 --> 00:02:12,903
She adds tracking,

48
00:02:12,903 --> 00:02:15,708
and the buyer's assistant reads it back.

49
00:02:18,045 --> 00:02:20,045
Shelfie turns a paper price list into

50
00:02:20,045 --> 00:02:22,820
a shop that any AI assistant can find,

51
00:02:22,820 --> 00:02:25,507
order from, and pay with PayPal.

52
00:02:25,507 --> 00:02:27,607
The money goes straight to the seller.

53
00:02:27,607 --> 00:02:28,908
Agent shopping shouldn't be

54
00:02:28,908 --> 00:02:30,958
only for shops with a website.

55
00:02:30,958 --> 00:02:34,225
For Rosa, a sheet of paper is enough.
